steps.human:
Run the selected registered query within trusted scope and budget. Keep canonical sources, exact field meanings and completeness limits with the results.

Schema, permission, version and budget checks remain decisive implementation checks; Jev cannot waive them.

Return these results to [Jev shared attempt comparison](docs/product-truth/flows/leafcutter/retrieve-project-knowledge.flow.json#compare), for every executed query, not only a newly built one. Nonaccepted inputs never reach this step.

Return this attempt and its limits to [shared attempt comparison](docs/product-truth/flows/leafcutter/retrieve-project-knowledge.flow.json#compare) alongside prior or complementary methods. The main route owns comparison, advisory recording and combination once.

I/O boundary: The operation remains example_ac_requirements across input/output. The partial result preserves the missing requested field; execution success does not settle the original need.

Contract fields and examples (generated)
Consumes:
  knowledge_request/operation: string (optional; default "get_entities")
  knowledge_request/operation_version: string (optional; default "1")
  knowledge_request/arguments: object (optional; default {})
  knowledge_request/revision: string (optional; default "latest")
  knowledge_request/budget: object (optional)
  Runtime contract: [knowledge_request](knowledge/contracts.py)
Produces:
  knowledge_result/operation: string (optional; default "")
  knowledge_result/operation_version: string (optional; default "1")
  knowledge_result/status: string (required)
  knowledge_result/source_sha: null|string (optional; default null)
  knowledge_result/generation_id: null|string (optional; default null)
  knowledge_result/evidence: array (optional; default [])
  knowledge_result/answer: null|object (optional; default null)
  knowledge_result/warnings: array (optional; default [])
  Runtime contract: [knowledge_result](knowledge/contracts.py)

PROPOSED - missing JSON binding (produces): Shared attempt result wrapper
